# requirements/ci-oracle.in -- CI oracle INTENT (input pin).
#
# This file expresses intent: which top-level package (and extras) the CI
# differential gate scripts/check_schema_oracle.py needs. It is NOT installed
# directly. pip-compile resolves it into requirements/ci-oracle.txt, the SINGLE
# canonical install artifact (fully pinned, hashed) that CI installs with
# `pip install --require-hashes`.
#
# Relationship:
#   ci-oracle.in   -> intention (one direct pin, no hashes)
#   ci-oracle.txt  -> canonical locked installation (all transitive deps + hashes)
#
# jsonschema is a differential REFERENCE only; it never enters the runtime/zipapp.
# Regenerate the lock with pip-tools on Python 3.12:
#   pip-compile --generate-hashes --no-emit-index-url \
#       --output-file=requirements/ci-oracle.txt requirements/ci-oracle.in
jsonschema[format]==4.26.0
